# Lesson 5, your Exercise 3, completed with East-West cards.
title: Your Exercise 3: partner shows hearts
id: L05-03
type: exercise
lesson: 5
concepts: 5.4
student: S
board: 5
dealer: N
vulnerable: NS

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  KQJ9   QT84   A6     KJ6
  E  843    KJ52   T2     A532
  S  T762   A7     KQ54   QT7
  W  A5     963    J9873  984

auction:
  N 1NT    = 15-17 points, balanced
  E Pass
  S 2C     = Stayman: do you have a 4-card major?
  W Pass
  N 2H     = Four hearts (maybe four spades too)
  E Pass
  S 3NT*   = Game values, four spades, not four hearts
     key: No heart fit. Stayman promised a major, so 3NT also tells North you have four spades.
     not 4H: You have only two hearts.
     not 3S: 3♠ shows five spades. You have four.
     not 2NT: 2NT only invites. With 11 points you have enough for game.
  W Pass
  N 4S     = I have four spades too
     key: North has both majors, so North corrects to 4♠.
  E Pass
  S Pass
  W Pass

auction recap:
  North's 2♥ showed four hearts, but you have only two. Since your 2♣ promised
  a 4-card major and it wasn't hearts, your 3NT told North you have four
  spades, with enough for game. North has four spades too, so North bids 4♠.
  North is declarer, because North bid spades first, and so East will lead to
  the first trick.

play:
  1   E DT  S D4  W D3  N DA
  2   N SK  E S3  S S2  W SA
      note: Start drawing trumps. West wins the ace.
  3   W D8  N D6  E D2  S DK
  4   S S6  W S5  N SQ  E S4
      note: Back in dummy, lead trumps again.
  5   N SJ  E S8  S S7  W D7
      note: The last trump: the opponents have none left.
  6   N H4  E H2  S HA  W H3
      note: Now the hearts, starting with dummy's ♥A.
  7   S H7  W H6  N HT  E HJ
      note: Give up the heart loser now, while you still control the other suits.
  8   E CA  S C7  W C4  N C6
  9   E C2  S CT  W C8  N CK
  10  N H8  E H5  S ST  W H9
      note: Ruff a heart in dummy.
  11  S DQ  W D9  N HQ  E C3
      note: Declarer throws the last heart on dummy's ♦Q.
  12  S CQ  W C9  N CJ  E C5
      note: Cash the ♣Q.
  13  S D5  W DJ  N S9  E HK
      note: Declarer ruffs the last diamond. 10 tricks: 4♠ made.

play recap:
  Declarer's plan: count losers first. The ♠A and ♣A must be lost, so only
  one heart can go. Dummy's ♥A covers one of declarer's four hearts. Of the
  other three, give one up, ruff one in dummy and throw one on dummy's ♦Q.
  Draw trumps first.

  4♠ made exactly. 3NT would also have made on this deal, with nine tricks,
  so the choice cost nothing this time. When you find a 4-4 major fit, the
  suit contract is usually at least as good as 3NT, and often better.
